On 3/21/06, Cyril Slobin <slobin@sksys.net> wrote:
> coi rodo
>
> Playing jboselkei, I was to comment the translation containing {ro
> nae'bo la djil noi zutse}. I am in doubt whether {noi zutse} applies
> only to {la djil} (as author of translation assumes) or to the whole
> sumti {ro na'ebo la djil} (as I guess)? Jbofi'e output is opaque.
>
> Which version is correct?

Only to {la djil}.

To get the other meaning, you need to use the LAhE/NAhE-BO
terminator, which is LUhU:

{ro na'e bo la djil lu'u noi zutse}

mu'o mi'e xorxes


